-- ============================================================
-- Marksmanship: Improved Hunter's Mark -- pet leech
-- ============================================================
--
-- TODO.md: "Improved Hunter's Mark also heals your pet for 10/20/30% of the
--  damage done to targets with Hunter's Mark."
--
-- YOUR damage only, not the pet's -- agreed explicitly.  30% of a hunter's
-- whole throughput is already a large heal, and keeping the pet's own damage
-- out means the talent reads as "you sustain your pet" rather than the pet
-- sustaining itself.
--
-- Both retail effects are kept intact (attack power bonus, mana cost); the
-- leech rides Effect3, which retail left empty.  Its base points 9/19/29 render
-- as 10/20/30 through the $s3 +1 rule, and the script reads the same value with
-- aurEff->GetAmount().
--
-- Why the aura is on the HUNTER and not the pet, unlike Focused Aim: the
-- triggering event is the hunter's own damage, so it already reaches the
-- hunter's aura list.  No spell_pet_auras plumbing is involved.
--
-- ------------------------------------------------------------
-- Three things about 200762 that are each load-bearing
-- ------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- 1. SPELL_ATTR1_NO_THREAT (AttributesEx 1024).  Healing normally forwards 50%
--    of the amount healed as assist threat to everything fighting the target --
--    Spell.cpp:2776 calls ForwardThreatForAssistingMe with `gain * 0.5f`.
--    Without this bit the talent would hand the HUNTER threat in direct
--    proportion to their own damage, actively fighting Pack Hunting, Focused Aim
--    and the whole pet-tanking design.  ThreatManager.cpp:757 short-circuits on
--    the attribute.
--
-- 2. DamageClass 0 (SPELL_DAMAGE_CLASS_NONE) and NO spell_bonus_data row.
--    Unit::SpellHealingBonusDone returns the amount untouched for a NONE-class
--    spell with no bonus row (Unit.cpp:9650), which is what keeps a
--    pre-computed share of damage from being re-scaled by spell power.  Note
--    this differs from the damage path, where the NONE early-return still
--    applies DoneTotalMod -- the reason Beast Cleave's 200739 needed
--    IGNORE_CASTER_MODIFIERS as well.
--
-- 3. AttributesEx3 537198592 = SUPPRESS_CASTER_PROCS (0x00010000)
--                            | ALWAYS_HIT            (0x00040000)
--                            | IGNORE_CASTER_MODIFIERS (0x20000000),
--    plus AttributesEx2 SPELL_ATTR2_CANT_CRIT (0x20000000).  SUPPRESS_CASTER_PROCS
--    matters most: without it a heal that procs off damage would be a proc
--    source itself.
--
-- EffectImplicitTargetA1 = 5 (TARGET_UNIT_PET) resolves
-- m_caster->GetGuardianPet() (Spell.cpp:1794), and the caster is the hunter --
-- the same targeting retail's Go for the Throat Focus payload uses.


